decisions:
  - id: tells-are-checks
    decision: Tells are checks with severity and per-repo overrides recorded in design-system.yaml, never global bans
    rationale: taste-skill hard-bans its author's taste (Inter, serifs, em dashes) for every brand; Atelier's premise is the creator's taste via boards and the brand cascade, so an informed pick must be able to override a tell with provenance.
  - id: tells-as-data
    decision: Catalog is YAML with detect.kind (count/literal/pattern/structure/review) and scope (landing/product/content)
    rationale: Lets Luna/Mika use it now and `atelier check` run the mechanical kinds later; scope keeps landing-page tells from firing on product UI, which taste-skill excludes entirely.
  - id: preserve-list
    decision: 'Redesign mode writes load-bearing names (routes, nav labels, form fields, analytics hooks, SEO surface) to a persistent preserve: list'
    rationale: taste-skill's 'never change silently' list only lives in one prompt; persisting it makes every later build and finish review respect it.
learnings:
  - 'Our own example design system taught the cliché (Fraunces + #f6f3ee cream + clay accent); example values in skill references get copied, so they must be non-default and labeled illustrative.'
  - taste-skill's research figures (skill discovery %, tip effects) are unsourced; not imported.
